FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/stdlib.rs:587 — `uppercase` (and `lowercase`/`trim`/`split`/`join` below it) matches only `args.first()` and never checks arity, so `say text.uppercase("a", "b")` answers `A` instead of refusing — a typo silently dropped, contradicting the phase's "refuses bad arguments by name" claim which pins too-many only for `list.map` — fix: require `args.len() == 1` (return `None` so `builtin` reports `was called with arguments it cannot use`) and add a too-many case for a flat-backed member.
2. [MAJOR] src/interpreter.rs:2071 — the expression-receiver path evaluates any receiver and answers `map` for any `Value::List`, while SPEC.md:1204 says "A list written out in full is the only one a `.` can be put in front of" — so `(xs).map(f)` or a call returning a list answers where bare `xs.map(f)` is refused, bypassing the round-8 refusal; the same holds at src/bytecode/vm.rs:2771 — fix: restrict the path to a list literal or broaden SPEC plus both gates; settles by running `set xs to [1, 2, 3]` then `say (xs).map(double)` on both engines.
3. [MINOR] phases/phase-050/REPORT.md:705 — pastes `git status --short` as `(empty)` after runs on a tree whose change set is the round's own two modified files (`phases/phase-050/REPORT.md`, `phases/phase-050/FINDINGS.md`), contradicting the Gates section's own "clean apart from this phase's own files" — a wrong sentence about the tree, the same class round 10 existed to fix — fix: paste the real status or qualify as empty apart from this phase's own files.
